{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy","id":1177212,"title":"Creative Imperial Thaumaturgy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-19T02:45:40-08:00","id":1177212,"title":"Creative Imperial Thaumaturgy","content":"My players are on the verge of archmastery (one of them is undergoing the Trials now), so I thought I would start a thread for creating imperial spells that work with 2nd Edition rules. These spells assume that the Arcane Beat and Mana cost from Imperial Mysteries is followed, and that the Practices are pretty much the same as listed in the book. Spells are Withstood instead of contested, of course. I don't expect there to be a ton of spells in here, but I'm curious to see what people can come up with.<br /> <br /> I'm also going with a few guidelines, which people might debate or have different opinions on: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mechanics for these spells are based on these <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kIDr9_-oBGLEPwmfmtTyTefnSh9d5D62LdY1fCa7UHI/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Imperial Mysteries 2e Update Rules</a>.</li> <li>The general idea of &quot;take the spell, make it a bit better, and have that be a Reach effect&quot; is still in effect. Similarly, Reach and Mana cost rules from the Creative Thaumaturgy section are followed (e.g. 2 Reach to affect spellcasting rolls).</li> <li>Dynamics spells can only propagate under conditions relevant to the Arcanum unless other Arcana are added to the spell. Some conditions may be general enough that they're not really attached to an Arcanum, and are unaffected by this rule. This assumption is mostly for stuff where there's a clear separation between the Arcanum purviews, like propagating a Mind Dynamics spell through the Internet or sympathetic connections. I would say that needs the assistance of Forces or Space.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> I will start with a simple Mind Dynamics spell, a memetic version of Psychic Reprogramming. It's pretty much a copy and paste of Psychic Reprogramming with the Dynamics rules tacked on.<br /> <br /> <b>Meme (Mind </b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022<b>)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Resolve</li> <li><b>Example Quintessence:</b> Editorial articles, Temenos realms related to the changes, a regal decree from a ancient, powerful monarch.</li> </ul><br /> The archmaster inflicts a mental rewiring that spreads by memetic means. Similar to the Psychic Reprogramming spell, the archmaster may change one of the following aspects of subjects for each Potency of the spell: Virtue, Vice, Short-Term Aspiration, Long-Term Aspiration, Obsession, a non-Physical Persistent Condition, or may move one dot between two Social Skills, or between two Mental Skills. The archmaster must choose the conditions under which the spell dynamically propagates or initially affects subjects. Most commonly, this is when an affected subject talks to or sees another person. When a subject is affected by the spell, they Withstand with Resolve, and the spell affects them for its entire Duration. Each subject is affected for the spell's Duration that was set when it was first cast. The spell remains under the archmaster's spell control until it expires from every subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Another Arcanum \u2022\u2022</b><b>: </b>The spell can propagate by dynamic conditions under the purview of the added Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster may also move dots between two Social Attributes, or two Mental Attributes per Potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The spell may inflict different changes on each subject it affects, as stipulated by conditions set when the spell is cast. For example, the archmaster may specify that people above a certain age get different Aspirations than those under that age.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The archmaster instead specifies a general goal or motive that affected subjects must try to achieve. In this case, the Storyteller decides what changes the spell inflicts on the subjects, but they must be in line with the archmaster's goals and wishes. This Reach effect is usually combined with the above Reach effect for maximum effectiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 01-22-2018, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T06:37:04-08:00","id":1177574,"title":"","content":"Here is another one based on descriptions in Imperial Mysteries.<br /> <br /> <b>Conscious Spell (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Resolve</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> An Imago, a Paradox created by the subject, Essence from a complex supernatural intelligence.</li> </ul><br /> The subject can create Imagos that react to conscious thought. While under the effects of this spell, the subject may use an Instant Action to transfer spell control of one more ongoing spells to another mage or a Sleepwalker. If the subject of Conscious Spell is mage, they also gain full conscious control over any spells under their control: In addition to being able to willingly lower Spell Factors, they can also raise them--but only to their original values if they were reduced in the first place.<br /> <br /> Spell Control cannot be transferred if it would put the target over their own Spell Control limit. This spell can transfer a number of spells up to Potency, although other abilities granted by this spell remain until its Duration expires. This spell is capable of transferring spell control of an Imperial spell to a lesser mage or even a Sleepwalker, but this is a breach of the Pax Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Spell Control can be transferred even if it would put the target over their Spell Control limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, the subject can also swap Spell Factors one-for-one, such as decreasing duration by one step to increase Potency by one. Such alterations cannot exceed Conscious Spell\u2019s Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, the subject can apply--but not remove--Reach effects to currently existing spells under their control. These may generic or spell-specific Reach effects. If applying Reach would cause the spell to exceed its controller\u2019s free Reach, the spell\u2019s controller must make a Paradox roll. This dice pool can be reduced with Mana, but the controller can only spend an amount up to their Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit. Paradox caused by this effect has the severity of an Imperial spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T13:30:40-08:00","id":1177671,"title":"","content":"I developed this spell for an archmaster NPC in my game. I'm not sure if I'm thinking about the Practices right though...<br /> <br /> Divine Avatar (Mind 6 + Prime 2)<br /> Practice: Dynamics?<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> This spell works like &quot;Possession&quot;, but casting it as an imperial spell allows the archmage to cast their magic through the vessel they are possessing. They use their normal spell casting rules to do so, and still flare their own nimbus.<br /> <br /> Reach +1: if the subject is a mage, pay 1 mana to use their nimbus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T14:31:48-08:00","id":1177688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1177671#post1177671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I developed this spell for an archmaster NPC in my game. I'm not sure if I'm thinking about the Practices right though...<br /> <br /> Divine Avatar (Mind 6 + Prime 2)<br /> Practice: Dynamics?<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> This spell works like &quot;Possession&quot;, but casting it as an imperial spell allows the archmage to cast their magic through the vessel they are possessing. They use their normal spell casting rules to do so, and still flare their own nimbus.<br /> <br /> Reach +1: if the subject is a mage, pay 1 mana to use their nimbus</div> </div> </div> </div>This spell could probably just be a +2 Reach option on the original Possession spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-20-2018, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T04:16:59-08:00","id":1177817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1177671#post1177671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I developed this spell for an archmaster NPC in my game. I'm not sure if I'm thinking about the Practices right though...<br /> <br /> Divine Avatar (Mind 6 + Prime 2)<br /> Practice: Dynamics?<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> This spell works like &quot;Possession&quot;, but casting it as an imperial spell allows the archmage to cast their magic through the vessel they are possessing. They use their normal spell casting rules to do so, and still flare their own nimbus.<br /> <br /> Reach +1: if the subject is a mage, pay 1 mana to use their nimbus</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that if the archmage is channeling their <i>own</i> magic through the vessel, then it's an Imperial spell. If it's just forcing the target to use their own magic, then that could be a Reach effect on the original spell.<br /> <br /> Here's a new spell. This time, from the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>Unerring Compass</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A compass Artifact from Pandemonium, an original copy of an arrest warrant for the subject.</li> </ul><br /> This spell provides the archmaster with unerring direction to what they seek. When cast on a subject, the archmaster knows the subject\u2019s exact location in the Tellurian. Unlike the lesser Locate Object spell, this spell also tells the archmaster exactly how to get to the subject\u2019s location, based on the archmaster\u2019s desired method of getting there (such as \u201cfastest way\u201d or \u201csubtlest way\u201d). The spell is capable of adjusting itself if the archmaster\u2019s desired method of approach changes. Thus, the archmage always knows exactly where to teleport, what alley to walk down, or what train to take. Concealing magic provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster is guaranteed to always have surprise in the first round of combat with, and always have the Edge in a chase with, the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T02:33:29-08:00","id":1178015,"title":"","content":"Here's another Mind spell. This time it's an Entities spell that allows the archmage to change XP costs for the target. Not sure if this is the right way to go about it though.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlightenment (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Entities</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 4 Mana, 2 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A memory where the subject learned something new related to the chosen categories, a symbol from the subject\u2019s Oneiros representing a desire to learn.</li> </ul><br /> The archmaster radically expands or alters the subject\u2019s ability to learn and process new information. The archmaster may change the cost the subject pays in Experiences in a single category, such as Skills, Merits, or Arcana. Each Arcanum counts as one category for this spell. Some categories are harder to adjust than others: the Potency of this spell converts directly to \u201cExperiences,\u201d and the archmaster must \u201cspend\u201d an amount equal to the category\u2019s base cost in order to adjust its cost by one. For example, four Potency is required to increase or decrease the Experience cost of an Arcanum by one. The minimum cost for a category cannot be reduced below 1 Experience.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster may split the spell\u2019s Potency to alter another category. This Reach effect can be applied multiple times to alter the Experience cost of multiple categories.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster can add to, remove from, or change the type of Experience required for the category. For example, the archmaster could make it so that the subject can only spend Arcane Experiences to gain Merits, or that they could spend any kind of Experiences to gain Merits. The type of Experience must be one the subject can spend. For an additional Reach and one point of Mana, the archmaster can substitute any type of Experience. This effect cannot remove the ability of the subject to spend Experiences completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:42:22-08:00","id":1178104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1177671#post1177671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell works like &quot;Possession&quot;, but casting it as an imperial spell allows the archmage to cast their magic through the vessel they are possessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly confident that a Mage should already be able to use their magic while possessing someone by spending the Reach for remote viewing a distant subject (via the possessed target's senses).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1178015#post1178015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Enlightenment (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the way you handled Potency on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-22-2018, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T02:50:18-08:00","id":1179470,"title":"","content":"Here is another Space spell. I am not really happy with its current mechanics. I would like suggestions on how to better implement a &quot;self-repairing Ward&quot; that don't involve too much screwing around with the Clash of Wills rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Autonomous Ward (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A literal shield used to save a man\u2019s life in a great battle, a heavily fortified compound</li> </ul><br /> <br /> This spell is similar to the Ward (Space \u2022\u2022) spell, but with the additional ability of being self-repairing and having dynamic Keys and conditions under which the Ward allows magic to pass through it. Like the regular spell, \u201cmagic that uses the sympathy of Warded subjects or attempts to warp Warded areas provokes a Clash of Wills\u201d and the archmaster knows when one of their wards is attacked. Any attack upon the Ward causes it to repair and adjust itself to make further incursion more difficult. If the ward is attacked by powers that it has been attacked by before, add the spell\u2019s Potency as a bonus to the Clash of Wills roll. Further, any effects that reduce the Spell Factors of the Ward are only temporary, assuming they didn\u2019t dispel the Ward outright. One scene after the Ward is affected, it returns to full strength.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a Key that allows use of Space magic on the Warded subject. This Key can be based on generalized, intuitive desires of the archmaster. <br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> &quot;The mage may cast Autonomous Ward upon an Iris or its Key, preventing the Iris from opening while the Ward remains in effect. Supernatural powers opening the Iris provoke a Clash of Wills.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:16:21-08:00","id":1179669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1179470#post1179470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is another Space spell. I am not really happy with its current mechanics. I would like suggestions on how to better implement a &quot;self-repairing Ward&quot; that don't involve too much screwing around with the Clash of Wills rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Autonomous Ward (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A literal shield used to save a man\u2019s life in a great battle, a heavily fortified compound</li> </ul><br /> <br /> This spell is similar to the Ward (Space \u2022\u2022) spell, but with the additional ability of being self-repairing and having dynamic Keys and conditions under which the Ward allows magic to pass through it. Like the regular spell, \u201cmagic that uses the sympathy of Warded subjects or attempts to warp Warded areas provokes a Clash of Wills\u201d and the archmaster knows when one of their wards is attacked. Any attack upon the Ward causes it to repair and adjust itself to make further incursion more difficult. If the ward is attacked by powers that it has been attacked by before, add the spell\u2019s Potency as a bonus to the Clash of Wills roll. Further, any effects that reduce the Spell Factors of the Ward are only temporary, assuming they didn\u2019t dispel the Ward outright. One scene after the Ward is affected, it returns to full strength.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a Key that allows use of Space magic on the Warded subject. This Key can be based on generalized, intuitive desires of the archmaster.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> &quot;The mage may cast Autonomous Ward upon an Iris or its Key, preventing the Iris from opening while the Ward remains in effect. Supernatural powers opening the Iris provoke a Clash of Wills.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Archmasters simply win Clashes, I'm not sure a healing rule is required, but...<br /> hmm...<br /> <br /> Yeah, just checked it: No rules for Clash dispelling the ward are in the base spell nor the general Clash rules.<br /> Weakening potency is a 1st ed. only thing, it appears.<br /> <br /> And a Ward by an Archmage is pretty darn near perfect Aegis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:42:12-08:00","id":1179687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1179669#post1179669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Archmasters simply win Clashes, I'm not sure a healing rule is required, but...<br /> hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Only against lesser beings. Against other archmages, Clashes are still relevant. Also probably relevant for Rank 6+ beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, just checked it: No rules for Clash dispelling the ward are in the base spell nor the general Clash rules.<br /> Weakening potency is a 1st ed. only thing, it appears. </div> </div> </div>It's true that weakening Potency is a first edition thing, unless a mage reduces Potency voluntarily. Dispel Magic simply suppresses the target spell (or destroys it outright, with Reach). So what to do with a self-repairing Ward? Perhaps any dispel magic spell that doesn't outright destroy the Ward is reduced to transitory duration, or perhaps is subject to &quot;dissonance&quot; so that it's eventually destroyed?<br /> <br /> As for Clash of Wills, the intent of that is for spells which do Clash with Ward. That wouldn't be Dispel Magic, but rather other Space spells for example. What I don't like is giving a bonus to the Clash of Wills, as that is not done at all in the core rules. Of course, part of the thing with archamages is bypassing some of those rules, but I don't want to go too crazy with that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a Ward by an Archmage is pretty darn near perfect Aegis. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good name for a spell. What would an Aegis do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:59:39-08:00","id":1179739,"title":"","content":"Given that the mechanic of decay is removed, I suggest a bonus to Clashes themselves that stacks with the normal factors. If that bonus worked a bit like Defense, it could recover every round to &quot;heal&quot; and multiple Clashes could wear it down, briefly, before it recovered. Spitballing, here, mind.<br /> <br /> Aegis as a Space effect could block Sympathetic and Ranged attacks. Supernatural effects that can target unfailingly or strike at range trigger a Clash. That would be a pretty darn good protection. Use Reach to add bans against other things like chemical or biological agents. Make it adjust retention or loss of heat and gasses on its own and you get it up to a Space 6 effect. Heck, it could have a Ban per Potency that optimize to fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T08:29:36-08:00","id":1185587,"title":"","content":"Here is a revised version of Autonomous Ward, as well as a first iteration of the Aegis spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Adaptive Ward (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A literal shield used to save a man\u2019s life in a great battle, a heavily fortified compound</li> </ul><br /> This spell is similar to the Ward (Space \u2022\u2022) spell, but with the additional ability of adjusting to block attacks and having dynamic Keys and conditions under which the Ward allows magic to pass through it. Like the regular spell, \u201cmagic that uses the sympathy of Warded subjects or attempts to warp Warded areas provokes a Clash of Wills\u201d and the archmaster knows when one of their wards is attacked. If the ward is attacked by powers that it has been attacked by before, add the spell\u2019s Potency as a bonus to the Clash of Wills roll. Each time the ward is attacked, during a Scene, this bonus is reduced by 1, down to a minimum of 0. At the end of the Scene, the bonus returns to full strength.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a Key that allows use of Space magic on the Warded subject. This Key can be based on generalized, intuitive desires of the archmaster.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The mage may cast Autonomous Ward upon an Iris or its Key, preventing the Iris from opening while the Ward remains in effect. Supernatural powers opening the Iris provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> Stuff</li> </ul><br /> The archmaster warps space in such a way that the affected subject or area is dynamically protected from passive and active harm. By reflexively warping space, all obvious attempts to harm the subject fail or are greatly penalized. The subject is completely protected from all mundane sources of obvious harm. Gunshots pass through or warp around the subject. If the subject would accidentally walk over a pit, a Ban would prevent the subject from falling in. Active supernatural attacks can still affect the subject, but trigger a Clash of Wills. The protection provided by Aegis is rather blunt. Passive, lingering dangers will cause the spell to form a Ban around the subject as long they remain in the area, which prevents interaction with the environment.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Any Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> By adding another Arcanum, the archmaster can fine-tune the Aegis. Any passive obvious phenomenon under the added Arcanum\u2019s purview that would be harmful to the subject is altered to be non-threatening. This lets subjects enter dangerous places such as the Lower Depths, exist indefinitely in the vacuum of space, and so on while still being able to interact with the environment.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster may specify a Key that allows magic to bypass the protection of the Aegis. This Key can be based on generalized, intuitive desires of the archmaster.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Aegis protects against one non-obvious phenomenon per level of Potency, such as invisible toxic gases. What is non-obvious is ultimately up to the Storyteller. The subject does not need to know about phenomena beforehand. When first encountered, the subject immediately learns of the harmful effect, and may choose to add it to the aegis\u2019 protection as a reflexive action at any point thereafter.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The dynamic spatial warping extends into the subject\u2019s sympathetic links as well, increasing the Withstand that must be overcome by the spell\u2019s Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The Aegis has enhanced protection against supernatural attacks. If a supernatural attack requires a dice pool to hit, it is penalized by the spell\u2019s Potency. This includes aimed spells, and affects a number of attacks equal to the spell\u2019s Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 02-16-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T13:06:32-08:00","id":1185708,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a more apt name for Autonomous ward would be Adaptive ward <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T15:18:12-08:00","id":1185742,"title":"","content":"I changed the name of Autonomous Ward to Adaptive Ward and also updated Aegis to be more in line with the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines. The penalizing of supernatural attack dice pools was moved to a +2 Reach effect since it can affect spellcasting rolls and supernatural powers. It also only works on a number of attacks equal to Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:49:41-08:00","id":1185846,"title":"","content":"Some more ideas that might be interesting:<br /> Life dynamics: Transform life, but the features change on the fly (Darwin from Marvel); Adaptive regeneration (Doomsday style)<br /> Fate dynamics: Oath, but the participants can be changed (Eg, hereditary oath); Law = Enforce a &quot;law&quot; within area, lawbreakers get Hexed (Ravnica guildpact). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T00:58:19-08:00","id":1185849,"title":"","content":"At first I though the Law spell would just be an area version of Sworn Oaths, but I guess the difference is that for Sworn Oaths the target has to take the Oath freely. But maybe you could do it with an AOE Fate Making spell? How does the Law spell fall under Dynamics? Maybe if the law could change...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 02-14-2018, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T02:33:40-08:00","id":1185861,"title":"","content":"Ah, the way i envisioned it, it would fall under dynamics because it contains a lot of parameters that could change:<br /> This is the way i envisioned it&gt;<br /> <br /> Setup:<br /> You make a body of laws for your personal fief, (which happens to contain provisions for changing the laws).<br /> And then cast Law to enforce it (On something the size of a country).<br /> Being immortal, you cast the spell with indefinite duration.<br /> <br /> Over the years, the law gets changed (to go with the times), so the spell would enforce the Law<br /> If the borders of the country expand, the law expands there.<br /> If people move to the country, they also become subject to the spell<br /> <br /> In terms of mechanics, i was thinking more Divine intervention, mixed with Strings of Fate<br /> <br /> It could also be fun to have statements like &quot;Crime doesn't pay&quot;: any money obtained from criminal activity gets &quot;lost&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T02:52:23-08:00","id":1185864,"title":"","content":"That would definitely fit Dynamics, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:19:41-08:00","id":1185922,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm sure some of the Essence Shaping of idigam could fit here, as well as Noble Numina that Acrozatarim wrote up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T03:11:10-08:00","id":1187256,"title":"","content":"Edit: An updated version of the Law spell suggested by MovingMind. There are some small changes to the text and an additional Reach effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Law (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> The original text of a law that has been amended</li> </ul><br /> This spell turns the archmaster\u2019s will into the law of the land. Fate enforces adherence to the law, and punishes those who break the limits that have been set. The archmaster must specify a clear body of law or rules, although it does not need to be written down. Subjects of the spell gain one Boon per Potency as long as they adhere to the law, and suffer one Hex per Potency once they have broken the law. This spell can also be used to enforce only Boons or Hexes, instead of both. Boons and Hexes expire when the spell\u2019s Duration ends.<br /> <br /> The spell is capable of responding to changes in conditions: if the body of original body of law allows for amendment, the spell enforces any altered versions of it. Further, if the law specifies an area of jurisdiction (such as a county or state), the spell is capable of altering its Scale factor if the area of jurisdiction changes. Law must be cast as an Area spell to change size dynamically, and its original Scale factor must cover the original area of jurisdiction.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Fate conspires to undo or make impossible any actions conflicting with the law. Any attempts to break the law, intentionally or otherwise, even mundane actions, trigger a Clash of Wills roll. On failure, the subject may not proceed, or fate undoes the action. Characters without relevant shielding magic contest with Supernatural Tolerance + Resolve.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Subjects of the spell have one Aspiration or Obsession replaced by one of the archmaster\u2019s design, based on conditions the archmaster chooses.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster knows when subjects of the spell break the rules set forth by the spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 02-21-2018, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T06:47:00-08:00","id":1188161,"title":"","content":"While I appreciate the effort that Falco put into the &quot;Archmage Patch,&quot; I feel like it's a little too conservative. Where Core is giving you a nudge and a wink while muttering something about &quot;unlimited free Reach,&quot; Falco is sweating over whether Archmages &quot;Imperial Armor&quot; is too strong to print (summary: it's barely more potent than regular mage armor in most cases).<br /> <br /> Archmages are allowed to be the godlike beings they are. They should have utter mastery over the common practices, not simply the improvements that already come naturally with higher gnosis and arcana. This is Archmage: think big.<br /> <br /> P.S. Just something I noticed: Falco lists Methuselahs as an example of a &quot;greater being&quot; (as opposed to a lesser being: vampire, werewolf, mage, etc...) Methuselahs are simply Elders that no longer suffer from memory loss and forced torpor (Fog of Eternity?). No template change is offered, and no direct power increase is granted. In fact, the question of Methuselahs having access to 6+ Disciplines was brought up and explicitly, strongly denied. So Methuselahs are still Vampires, not Archvampires: as such, a Methuselah is &quot;simply&quot; a really strong, really old Vampire -- but still a Vampire, and classifies as a &quot;lesser being&quot; along with other Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 02-21-2018, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T07:23:03-08:00","id":1188166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1187256#post1187256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Fate conspires to undo or make impossible any actions conflicting with the law. Any attempts to break the law, intentionally or otherwise, trigger a Clash of Wills roll. On failure, the subject may not proceed, or fate undoes the action. Characters without relevant shielding magic contest with Supernatural Tolerance + Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane actions are not supposed to trigger Clash of Wills. This is imperial magic so you could break that rule, but in such case it should be clarified in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T07:30:27-08:00","id":1188169,"title":"","content":"Since this is purely a Fate spell (and therefore lacking Time's editing of the past, or Mind's control of actions) I'm seeing the Clash of Wills as more of a pre-emptive thing. In other words, the Clash of Wills happens before the mundane action, in order to allow/prevent the mundane action from ever taking place.<br /> <br /> If I want to fire a gun, and firearms are against the &quot;Law,&quot; I need to CoW and win before I draw and shoot - if I lose the CoW, my gun no long has bullets, or it has mysteriously disappeared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T07:33:01-08:00","id":1188170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188161#post1188161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Methuselahs are still Vampires, not Archvampires: as such, a Methuselah is &quot;simply&quot; a really strong, really old Vampire -- but still a Vampire, and classifies as a &quot;lesser being&quot; along with other Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the two explicit Methuselahs we're shown, one has three bodies and the other can tell a lie that reality conspires to make true. Both are ancients who had to &quot;die&quot; a second time to become what they are and one of the principal distinguishing factors of a Methuselah is no longer a consistent facet of the setting. <a href=\"http://blog.fantasyheartbreaker.com/2010/08/18/requiem-for-methuselahs/\" target=\"_blank\">They occupy the same niche as archmasters do and possess unusual qualities not exhibited by other vampires.</a> There is room to treat them with a similar level of consideration in a game where they're likely to cross paths with an archmage directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T08:00:33-08:00","id":1188174,"title":"","content":"&quot;<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">I was also pleased that </span></span></span><i>Requiem</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> did away with godlike elders.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;At the same time, I didn\u2019t want to break the mechanical ecology of <i>Requiem</i>, or drown player characters in unbeatable bad guys. And Lord, Lord did I never want to introduce 6+ dot Disciplines.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">So Zagreus has a broad range of abilities at high levels, but doesn\u2019t exceed **other elders**, or advanced player characters, in any specific field. His only really unusual number is Blood Potency, and play experience shows that the amount of Vitae a character can store and spend becomes a game of diminishing returns.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Emphasis mine)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Both quotes by Rose Bailey - and, it should be noted, Zegreus is the vampire (o</span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">ne of the two Methuselahs) </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">that can tell a lie which reality conspires to make true. Which really is nothing out of the ordinary for a high-level Devotion.<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that both Elder and Methuselah are references to *age* and is just a logical continuation of the titles... if anything, this continuation shows that Methuselahs are still within Vampire, and not their own template. Greater beings are named after something they *became* e.g. Deathlord, Archmage, True Fae. An Elder becoming a Methuselah is like an Adept becoming a Master: just a graduation in power within the scope of the template, not becoming a new one. The above emphasis even seems to imply that Methuselahs ARE still Elders, but with memories intact)<br /> <br /> They share the same niche insofar as both Elders/Methuselahs and Archmages are both 1) powerful, and 2) reclusive - this, as you and I both know, doesn't make them both &quot;Greater Beings.&quot; It requires far more than that to cross the gap.<br /> <br /> The one thing that you pointed out - Methuselahs having to die in a mystical ritual or circumstance, and mysteriously return to life - is an interesting point. It is a literal interpretation of the symbolic death and resurrection that mages endure to become archmages. So while I agree they have similarities, I don't think you can make the case for Methuselahs being a &quot;greater being&quot; along with Archmages, Rank 6+ Spirits, True Fae, Deathlords, and their ilk. They are still bound to the same physical body, they still function almost completely the same as &quot;normal&quot; Vampires, and they have no access to Disciplines 6+.<br /> <br /> As Rose said, they have time to master a huge array of abilities, but they don't exceed elders in a specific field. They just have a lot of them.<br /> <br /> Being a first among equals doesn't put them in a position to be bargaining with Archmages, Deathlords, and True Fae. All three require a template change. Methuselahs are the Vampire template with one bonus - thus, are still the Vampire template - thus, lesser beings.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 02-21-2018, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T11:10:39-08:00","id":1188235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188166#post1188166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mundane actions are not supposed to trigger Clash of Wills. This is imperial magic so you could break that rule, but in such case it should be clarified in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>This Reach effect was to cover the suggestion that was originally given about &quot;Crime doesn't pay,&quot; where stolen money would just disappear or something like that. But Fate magic doesn't usually work like that. Instead it screws with probabilities, and a chain of occurrences can bring about a specific event a Fate mage wants to happen. Narratively, and especially with imperial magic, it might start warping probability in such a way that things do straight up disappear or the like. But the Reach effect may &quot;allow&quot; someone to commit a crime against the Law, but conspire to undo it just as quickly. It's all about how the ST wants to play it.<br /> <br /> As for the text, yes. A few words added should clarify it properly.<br /> <br /> Edit: The spell has been updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 02-21-2018, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T13:14:07-08:00","id":1188276,"title":"","content":"What would you even Clash with? The systems for CoW don't support mundane actions at all.<br /> <br /> Would you just roll the dicepool of the action you attempted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T14:48:56-08:00","id":1188307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188276#post1188276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you even Clash with? The systems for CoW don't support mundane actions at all.<br /> <br /> Would you just roll the dicepool of the action you attempted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the spell specifies Supernatural Tolerance + Resolve. But yes, the system for Clash of Wills normally does not support this. But luckily archmages dabble in the impossible regularly. If there is a better way to achieve the same effect, I am open to suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T15:04:47-08:00","id":1188312,"title":"","content":"Which, incidentally, could very well mean the transgressor gets a higher dice pool for doing it mundanely. Especially considering that most major splats have their powers capped at five but Attributes can go up to ten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T18:45:54-08:00","id":1188364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188161#post1188161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate the effort that Falco put into the &quot;Archmage Patch,&quot; I feel like it's a little too conservative. Where Core is giving you a nudge and a wink while muttering something about &quot;unlimited free Reach,&quot; Falco is sweating over whether Archmages &quot;Imperial Armor&quot; is too strong to print (summary: it's barely more potent than regular mage armor in most cases).<br /> <br /> Archmages are allowed to be the godlike beings they are. They should have utter mastery over the common practices, not simply the improvements that already come naturally with higher gnosis and arcana. This is Archmage: think big.<br /> <br /> P.S. Just something I noticed: Falco lists Methuselahs as an example of a &quot;greater being&quot; (as opposed to a lesser being: vampire, werewolf, mage, etc...) Methuselahs are simply Elders that no longer suffer from memory loss and forced torpor (Fog of Eternity?). No template change is offered, and no direct power increase is granted. In fact, the question of Methuselahs having access to 6+ Disciplines was brought up and explicitly, strongly denied. So Methuselahs are still Vampires, not Archvampires: as such, a Methuselah is &quot;simply&quot; a really strong, really old Vampire -- but still a Vampire, and classifies as a &quot;lesser being&quot; along with other Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to keep them at about the same level as 1e, I wasn't reinventing the wheel, as mentioned, it's a patch.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Methuselah as we currently have them are weak and underexplored, but<br /> 1) I'd still call them just barely powerful enough to be able to, at least, Clash with an Archmage. The archmage is still likely much more powerful than them in the majority of ways. As Satchel pointed out, they DO have some minor 'break the template rules' abilities and they're said to be something on another level, so I think that they can Clash, even if i'd never call them (as they currently are) on the same power tier.<br /> Edit: To put it simpler, Mages are far more powerful than Vampires, and Archmages are far more powerful than Methuselahs, but you'd still let a Vamp clash a mage and still let the Methuselah Clash the Archmage.<br /> 2) I tend to treat MEthuselahs as gods myself, and that tends to influence my homebrew 'fluff', I'll admit. I give them a new template, some inherent abilities, and free access to custom powers that further twist their template. I'm currently running a crossover game over skype/discord and the city's Methuselah is a force of nature that's just starting to wake up again as part of their current plot. Fun times.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a separate note, I'm glad to see people making use of that document!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 02-21-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:54:32-08:00","id":1188396,"title":"","content":"Different supernaturals just have different methods of \u2018transcendence,\u2019 so to speak. For mages it involves literally rewriting reality. For werewolves it involves hitting the limit and just keep on going. For Beasts, it involves incarnating your own mythos. For vampires, it involves waking up even after everything you once loved die. And so on. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d argue that the following entities are on the tier that allow them to Clash Wills normally with archmages: Rank 6+ ephemerals, elder vampires from TYoN (those old enough to get their advanced Clan Curses), werewolves who became \u201cboddhisattvas of the hunt\u201d (Primal Urge 10 and beyond), Redeemed Prometheans, True Fae, Bound who reached their \u2018endgames\u2019 as teased in the Open Development blogs, mummies who reached Apotheosis, demons who fully unlocked their Ciphers, Beasts who attained Inheritance (not just Incarnation), and etc.<br /> <br /> Yes, some if not all of the above are pathetic in terms of power level. But everyone is when compared to archmages anyway, so I went for the \u2018existential\u2019 tiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:24:00-08:00","id":1188426,"title":"","content":"Fog of Ages isn't even a thing in 2E, so whatever 2E Methusalehs are, it's not just 'an elder immune to the Fog of Ages'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T02:21:12-08:00","id":1188439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188312#post1188312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, incidentally, could very well mean the transgressor gets a higher dice pool for doing it mundanely. Especially considering that most major splats have their powers capped at five but Attributes can go up to ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. Perhaps a Withstand is better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T02:26:33-08:00","id":1188440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188364#post1188364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a separate note, I'm glad to see people making use of that document!</div> </div> </div> </div>The patch is quite useful. I have revised the rules slightly for my own use (things like changing around the Reach costs for Imperial factors, adding more rules to the Cintamani, and some other minor stuff). It's a very good foundation to build on!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T11:32:53-08:00","id":1188584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188364#post1188364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried to keep them at about the same level as 1e, I wasn't reinventing the wheel, as mentioned, it's a patch.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Methuselah as we currently have them are weak and underexplored, but<br /> 1) I'd still call them just barely powerful enough to be able to, at least, Clash with an Archmage. The archmage is still likely much more powerful than them in the majority of ways. As Satchel pointed out, they DO have some minor 'break the template rules' abilities and they're said to be something on another level, so I think that they can Clash, even if i'd never call them (as they currently are) on the same power tier.<br /> Edit: To put it simpler, Mages are far more powerful than Vampires, and Archmages are far more powerful than Methuselahs, but you'd still let a Vamp clash a mage and still let the Methuselah Clash the Archmage.<br /> 2) I tend to treat MEthuselahs as gods myself, and that tends to influence my homebrew 'fluff', I'll admit. I give them a new template, some inherent abilities, and free access to custom powers that further twist their template. I'm currently running a crossover game over skype/discord and the city's Methuselah is a force of nature that's just starting to wake up again as part of their current plot. Fun times.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a separate note, I'm glad to see people making use of that document!</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I want to thank you for the effort you put into the Archmage Patch. It's a document that I deeply appreciate. Even if I don't see precisely eye-to-eye with you - overall it's groovy, and something I'll probably put to use.<br /> <br /> As far as Methuselahs are concerned, I'll sum up my position as succinctly as I can. There are two major obstacles to calling Methuselah's a &quot;Greater Being&quot; -- one is mechanical, and one is thematic:<br /> <br /> A) Mechanical: They have no access to Disciplines 6+<br /> B) Thematic: Requiem specifically and intentionally avoids transcendent Vampires which are &quot;godlike beings.&quot; (In my estimation, &quot;godlike&quot; = &quot;greater being&quot;)<br /> <br /> In every case of a &quot;lesser being&quot; becoming a &quot;greater being&quot; they experience a fundamental, relational shift to their reality. They abide by a new template, new rulesets, new relationships with themselves, with their Orders/Covenants/Political Groups, even with the Supernal (or equivalent) itself. Their change is dramatic, the scope of their influence hugely enlarged.<br /> <br /> Methuselahs simply don't have a fundamental shift. They actually lose something, albeit what they lose is a weakness. This is in harmony with the theme of what the Vampires ascended form actually is: being Human once again. Their &quot;Gondcala&quot; (forgive the spelling mistake), their second Embrace, is the embrace of Humanity mixed with Vampire: a being that doesn't have the innate weaknesses of Vampire, but also retains their strengths. Methuselah is one step on the journey of becoming more like a Human once again, as they lose the weakness of memory loss / memory disruption, yet retain all their former abilities.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, this isn't adding powers; it's taking away weakness. To climb the ladder, they don't add to the &quot;good&quot; so much as shed away the &quot;bad.&quot; And it aligns perfectly with the theme of what it means for a Vampire, specifically a Vampire, to ascend.<br /> <br /> Note that, again, the idea of a Cain-like supervampire, an &quot;Archvampire&quot; if you will, was present in Vampire: The Masquerade but noticably, intentionally absent in Requiem. This was fully intentional. What it MEANS to be &quot;transcendent&quot; to a vampire is fundamentally different to a Vampire than it is to a Mage.<br /> <br /> I don't see why there is an arms race between Archmage and Methuselahs anyway. They can't, and don't need to be, equals. Nothing is truly equal; there is only more power, and less power. Vampires indisputably start with far more impressive powers and resilience than a 1 gnosis, 2 arcana mage. Mages do, however, outpace them in growth. It's a different game line with different themes and different powers.<br /> <br /> If anything, I'd say that Vampires grow into something Other when they fall further and further into darkness; these beings are far stranger than Methuselahs, who in general wear the trappings of humanity. These Other beings are what the bloodlines are *becoming* - monsters that are as different from Vampires as Vampires are from humans. Gangrel seem to create the most of these strange beings, but all bloodlines have the capability. I'd argue that Mr. Three Bodies, the second example of Methuselah that Satchel mentioned, isn't a Methuselah at all -- unlike Zagreus, who is much like an Elder but without memory loss, Mr. Three Bodies is actually far stranger than a normal Vampire: he is what happens when a bloodline advanced past the known borders.<br /> THIS is probably an example of a &quot;Greater Being&quot; as far as Vampires are concerned, except it's not greater in any sense but raw power. It's actually far more hopeless than a normal Vampire.<br /> He even, if I remember correctly, referred to his former Vampiric state as being &quot;once a man&quot; -- as in, in comparison to what he is NOW, being a Vampire is being a Human. He's fallen that far.<br /> Obviously having three bodies gives him a new template, so that's my version of a &quot;Greater Being.&quot; Note that he is no longer a Vampire, or a Methuselah. He became Other.<br /> <br /> Now, strictly from a mechanical point of view, this Other is probably going to cap out in power at about an Archmage at 6 dots. They are stronger than normal, and classify as a Greater Being, but they don't have nearly the access to the growth potential that an Archmage has, nor the reality-bending powers. They would have a wide degree of Disciplines they have mastered, plus some new template-exclusive powers similar to Legacy Attainments, varying depending on what bloodline they are. Disciplines 6+ do not add new abilities, but do strengthen the dice pool for skills 1-5 of each Discipline line.<br /> <br /> One should always keep in mind that Vampires are a gameline focused on &quot;Personal Horror and Visceral Drama.&quot; Greater Beings are overwhelmingly &quot;tier 4&quot; cosmic events in scope, and deal with lofty, philosophical, time-and-space adventuring drama. To create a Vampire that attains the same power-level as an Archmage or Rank 6+ spirit bucks against the very essence of what makes Vampire Vampire.<br /> <br /> So while we disagree on the &quot;level of being&quot; that Methuselahs are (just to clarify, I still place Methuselah as firmly a lesser being, as they are still Vampires and not an advanced subtype) I can agree that even a theoretical Greater Being Vampire wouldn't hold a stick to a 7-10 dot Archmage. Not only would making that kind of Vampire be impossible with Disciplines 6+, but it would also destroy the theme of Vampire itself.<br /> <br /> But it's your game. Do what thou will. But as far as canon goes, Disciplines 6+ don't exist, and Methuselahs seem to be, according to Rose, purely in the realm of &quot;Elder Vampire&quot; and not &quot;Ascended, New Template Vampire.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T11:39:11-08:00","id":1188585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188426#post1188426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fog of Ages isn't even a thing in 2E, so whatever 2E Methusalehs are, it's not just 'an elder immune to the Fog of Ages'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are immune to memory loss, having a razor sharp memory. They intentionally do not have Disciplines 6+ dots. they intentionally are created to NOT be an &quot;unbeatable bad guy,&quot; they are meant to have a wide variety of fields mastered instead of breaking barriers in one particular area. They are intentionally not copying Archmage, which do indeed have Arcana 6+. are essentially unbeatable for Mages, and go deeply past normal supernaturals in their chosen fields. <br /> <br /> Elder Vampires are not greater beings, and Methuselahs are - are - Elder Vampires, who have died to one weakness. The change is significant, but not template-altering, transcendent change. It's like a Vampire who must now feed on other Vampires instead of feeding on humans: the change is significant, and has significant implications, but is not template-altering. <br /> <br /> Yes, losing a weakness isn't exactly the same as altering a requirement, but both changes are hardly what it means to become a greater being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:09:52-08:00","id":1188604,"title":"","content":"Vampires do not have memory problems in 2E. <br /> <br /> Methusalehs are not just Elder vampires that are 'immune' to a 'weakness'. We don't know what they are in 2E, but we do know that that is not it. Vampires do not have that particular weakness for them to be immune to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:26:50-08:00","id":1188611,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it would be better to take the discussion of elder vampires and Methuselahs to a different thread? The primary purpose of this thread is to come up with Imperial spells for use in 2e archmage games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:42:13-08:00","id":1188618,"title":"","content":"Since that is the case, we only have TYoN to go off, and therefore Methuselahs may not even exist. There are just Elders. <br /> <br /> What kinda baffles me is that many people look at Mage and envy their growth potential, but ignore the fact that Mages start out by far the weakest. <br /> Put a 1 gnosis, 2 life Mage vs a 1 harmony, 2 [whatever] werewolf in a cage, and see who wins. 99/100 times, it's going to be the werewolf. How is that balanced? It's not. Werewolves, just by virtue of being Werewolves, start off with hugely powerful, linear shapeshifting forms, and a slew of reflexive powers. They have so much raw power that they literally can tear a beginning mage or vapire to pieces. The tables turn when you dumb 500xp into each template, however. Mages start off the weakest, but end up the strongest. <br /> <br /> Where does Vampire fit in? They are the happy medium. While they don't start with the raw potency of Werewolf, they are nowhere near as frail as a Mage. Their growth is sharply linear, scaling well with experience. But they don't &quot;cap off&quot; as high as a Mage; they got part of their cake right from character creation, having innate Vampiric powers that put starting Mages to shame. <br /> <br /> Werewolf / Vampire // Mage<br /> <br /> Mage / Vampire // Werewolf <br /> <br /> The tables turn, slowly - and Vampires have the middle ground at all levels of play. <br /> <br /> If you want the growth potential of Mage, you should be prepared to give up the innate advantages of Vampire. <br /> <br /> But I'm digressing -- this is not World of Warcraft, where the primary engine and much of the fun comes from combat. Mage, Werewolf, and Vampire are games of roleplaying, not necessarily combat, and the fun is found in many avenues. All game lines are thematic and have unique situations. It happens that Mages are students of Supernal Magic, and Supernal Magic has virtually no limit; the limitation is found within the Mage herself. As the Mage grows in competency, her magic becomes strong and better. The growth potential of a Mage outstrips Werewolf and Vampire by definition; even as Werewolves and Vampires by definition have innate advantages that serve to empower them at all stages of the game, but especially early game. Giving them an advanced template is unnecessary, anti-thematic, and frankly doesn't fit with the overall schematic: Mages start off with nothing but magic, and end with all things magic, and that magic is essentially unlimited power -- Vampires and Werewolves can reach the limits of their respective power sources, but those power sources aren't as deep or potent as Supernal Magic. They are top-heavy, The Blood and Essence, giving you a nice fat slice of cake right off the bat, but their cake eventually runs out, whereas Mages get a thin slice to begin but are at an &quot;all you can eat&quot; buffet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:44:04-08:00","id":1188620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188611#post1188611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it would be better to take the discussion of elder vampires and Methuselahs to a different thread? The primary purpose of this thread is to come up with Imperial spells for use in 2e archmage games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like to see some 7 and 8 dot Imperial Magic spells. So far, the emphasis has been 6 dots spells (understandable, since that is what you're going to be dealing with in the immediate future). 7 is pretty wild, and 8 really starts to dig into some esoteric stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T13:51:36-08:00","id":1188650,"title":"","content":"As someone who doesn\u2019t have the Changeling previews from the Kickstarter, how does the Hedge work in 2E? Manipulating its thorns and Trods would be an Entities spell, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Grammar 02-22-2018, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T17:17:21-08:00","id":1188715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188650#post1188650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who doesn\u2019t have the Changeling previews from the Kickstarter, how does the Hedge work in 2E? Manipulating its thorns and Trods would be an Entities spell, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedgespinning operates by performing mundane actions thematically related to your desired outcome at a penalty and spending Glamour to allocate excess successes among effects; the Hedge also shapes itself in response to stimuli, and &quot;the Thorns&quot; is essentially the common name for &quot;the regions of the Hedge which are especially dangerous.&quot; Getting anywhere without following a trod calls for navigation rolls with a goal in mind, which is handled using a variant of the Chase mechanics, in which the Hedge itself is always a participant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T20:21:16-08:00","id":1188760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188650#post1188650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who doesn\u2019t have the Changeling previews from the Kickstarter, how does the Hedge work in 2E? Manipulating its thorns and Trods would be an Entities spell, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go back and forth between Dynamics and Entities. On one hand, you're effectively rewriting your own template (or the hedge itself) to make the hedge respond to it. On the other, one could argue a dynamics spell could 'account for' the myriad whims of the Wyrd in the hedge and allow some level of shaping a trod for a non-fae entity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T20:36:48-08:00","id":1188763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188760#post1188760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd go back and forth between Dynamics and Entities. On one hand, you're effectively rewriting your own template (or the hedge itself) to make the hedge respond to it. On the other, one could argue a dynamics spell could 'account for' the myriad whims of the Wyrd in the hedge and allow some level of shaping a trod for a non-fae entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combined with Satchel\u2019s comment, it seems likely that creating a trod is Dynamics, while changing how the Hedge responds to non-trod navigation is Entities. <br /> <br /> That, and there\u2019s always \u201cinstant Goblin Debt gain/loss\u201d for Entities/Excision. <br /> <br /> Ooh, another idea. Fae-Touched are still formed by their promise to a changeling, right? What would happen if a Fate Entities spell turns a normal person into one? Would one of the person\u2019s beloved get retroactively taken to Faerie, much to the local Gentry\u2019s amusement? Would avoiding this side effect be a Reach effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T21:22:34-08:00","id":1188773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188763#post1188763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combined with Satchel\u2019s comment, it seems likely that creating a trod is Dynamics, while changing how the Hedge responds to non-trod navigation is Entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that making a place part of a trod is something changelings, True Fae, Huntsmen, and the Hedge itself can accomplish, albeit with slightly more difficulty or preparation than using the environment to do the impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ooh, another idea. Fae-Touched are still formed by their promise to a changeling, right? What would happen if a Fate Entities spell turns a normal person into one? Would one of the person\u2019s beloved get retroactively taken to Faerie, much to the local Gentry\u2019s amusement? Would avoiding this side effect be a Reach effect? </div> </div> </div>The tricky part here is that the connection that makes a fae-touched can be passed along, usually to family members, if it doesn't lead to the original party going into the Hedge within their own lifetime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T21:43:37-08:00","id":1188775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1188773#post1188773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that making a place part of a trod is something changelings, True Fae, Huntsmen, and the Hedge itself can accomplish, albeit with slightly more difficulty or preparation than using the environment to do the impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, then Making could do it I guess. Oh well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The tricky part here is that the connection that makes a fae-touched can be passed along, usually to family members, if it doesn't lead to the original party going into the Hedge within their own lifetime. </div> </div> </div>The part where the \u2018touch\u2019 can be passed along is new to me. <br /> <br /> So maybe the Entities spell creates a \u2018static\u2019 connection by default, made transferable by Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T23:57:37-08:00","id":1188791,"title":"","content":"So:<br /> <br /> <b>Seed of The Wyrd (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Entities</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 4 Mana</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Composure</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A gift from an Old One, the blessing of a local freehold, proof of outsmarting a goblin marketeer, paying off the debt of a goblin queen</li> </ul><br /> By weaving aspects of the Wyrd itself into a subject's pattern, the Hedge becomes receptive to them in the same way it might be to fae beings. After the casting of the spell, the character is treated as having Wyrd 1 and Clarity 3 for the purpose of navigating the hedge, hedgespinning, and otherwise imposing their will or goals on the Hedge, and are treated like a Changeling for the sake of any limitations. Note that the effective Wyrd does not apply to anything else, including Supernatural Tolerance or Potency. These changes are Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell's potency can be split between additional effective Wyrd and additional effective Clarity, up to the normal maximums<br /> <br /> <br /> It's a bit clumsy as I don't have all my books on me at the moment, but there's a rough entities spell for you<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 02-23-2018, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:14:26-08:00","id":1188805,"title":"","content":"Entities and Excision spells are actually always Lasting. They're direct, permanent alterations to the target. The spell otherwise looks good. Maybe add another Reach effect to increase the Wyrd/Clarity (either 1 Reach per increase, or only 1 Reach to increase it once, similar to how you can apply a Reach when creating a ghost to go from Rank 1 to Rank 2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T04:14:33-08:00","id":1188826,"title":"","content":"Ah I had forgotten that; as I'd said, didn't have my book onhand. Made a minor tweak for now and might redo the reach later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:43:42-08:00","id":1190806,"title":"","content":"How's this one look?I hope nobody else has written up such a spell already.<br /> <br /> <b>Dynamic Rote (Any Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Total Arcanum dots of all Arcana used in the spell being scribed (Dynamic Arcana default to 5 for this total)</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> The first draft of a published work, the last remaining copy of a published work, an editied version of a published work that was never printed.</li> </ul><br /> By weaving the practice of Dynamics into a Rote as it is formed (this spell must be cast during the use of the Create Rote Attainment), the Mage can create a truly wondrous Rote which can adapt to the circumstances as needed.<br /> While incapable of creating Rotes for the Imperial Practices, these dynamic Rotes can modify their Rote Skills and Practices within their original Arcana as required.<br /> This Dynamism will only extend however to such Arcana as the Archmaster has achieved the Practice of Dynamics with, all other Arcana included in the spell will not be able to be modified in application.<br /> <br /> For example, an Archmaster who has achieved Dynamics with Prime could forge a dynamic Eidolon Rote which could transform into any other Prime Rote.<br /> If the Archmaster also had Mastery in Mind, then this original Rote could also include the potential for the creation of a Psyche within this Eidolon, as well as any other Prime creation the Archmage creates as they dynamically shift their Prime-Arcana. However at this point the 'Mind' element could not be changed, meaning it could only be used to create a Psyche within whatever Prime effect the dynamic rote creates.<br /> However if the Archmaster had achieved Dynamics with Mind, then the Rote could shift both its expression of Prime and Mind to any form it desires.<br /> <br /> While the Rote's creation will be Lasting, the Rote's dynamism will only last for the duration of the spell. When the spell ends, the Rote will remain in whatever form it is at that time, and any attempts to copy the Rote into a Grimoire will 'merely' create whatever Rote it is at that point (unless a further use of Dynamics is made upon the Scribed Grimoire).<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the creator is Mad, then the Rote may shift across any Arcana so long as it involves their 'specialist' Practice<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcana (Any \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022): </b>The Rote may be created to accomodate the ability to include any other Dynamic Arcana the Archmaster knows, including Arcana not used in the initial form of the spell (however these will contribute to Withstand).<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Arcana (Prime \u2022):</b> The Archmaster may immediately create a Grimoire containing his Dynamic spell, rather than imbuing the Rote he has learned with Dynamism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Clarity of example 03-02-2018, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T01:26:06-08:00","id":1190922,"title":"","content":"That's a very cool spell. Shouldn't the Mind example say &quot;archmastery in Mind,&quot; since the dynamism only works with arcana that the archmaster has?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T01:33:49-08:00","id":1190925,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, my example perhaps wasn't quite as clear as I had thought.<br /> Firstly it's Prime 6 where it can change to any Prime spell.<br /> Then it's Prime 6, Mind 5 where the Prime can change but the Mind can't.<br /> Then it's Prime 6, Mind 6 where both Arcana can shift as required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T02:45:08-08:00","id":1190930,"title":"","content":"When i read the spell, i thought of a rote that can be learnt by non archmages, as opposed to a Rote that can be cast by an archmage<br /> <br /> Maybe one where the Rote skill changes, i.e. one that has a flexible imago that adapts to the caster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T04:43:57-08:00","id":1190943,"title":"","content":"An archmage could use a Prime dynamics spell that assists in rote spell creation such that anyone who learns the rote can use any Skill they want when casting it.<br /> <br /> Having a rote that can change its Imago and thus cast basically any spell (i.e. apply Mudras yantra to any spellcasting) could also be Dynamics, but I would say such a benefit only lasts as long as the spell does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T04:20:30-07:00","id":1196008,"title":"","content":"A Prime spell, this time it is Dominions. Some people might argue that this is Excision, which is definitely a possibility. In the old edition, it is definitely excision. I picked Dominions, because mages' connection to the Supernal always seems to relate to the soul and the astral, which is a world of its own. Given that it is an assault directly against a mage's supernatural being, it departs from the normal creative thaumaturgy guidelines and is Withstood by Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <b>Annihilate Supernality</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dominions</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Gnosis</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 6 Mana, 5 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> ???</li> </ul><br /> One of the most feared tools of the Imperial Masters. This spell inverts and destroys the alterations made to a mage\u2019s soul when they Awakened, effectively un-Awakening them. This spell removes the mage template from the subject. The subject becomes a Sleepwalker. Any mage-only merits are refunded through Sanctity of Merits. The archmaster must have Prime at 8 dots and have at least the same amount of dots as the target in the appropriate Path Arcana in order to undo the Awakening. Otherwise, this spell can only disrupt an Awakening in progress. This spell cannot undo an archmage\u2019s Threshold Seeking.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The internal metaphysics of the target are so thoroughly annihilated that the subject becomes a Sleeper again. The entirety of their time as a mage is immediately affected by Quiessence, and without proper precautions, will cause the target to become irrevocably insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 03-21-2018, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:03:21-07:00","id":1196012,"title":"","content":"Having both Ruling Arcana at 5 is enough. Prime 8 is hugely dominant in Supernal superiority, and so having equal or greater knowledge to the Mage in his own Ruling Path + Prime 8 can believably sever the connection. <br /> <br /> Requiring that three Arcana be 8 is such an insane requirement for a spell that effectively works on Mages only. Remember, Archmage's souls cannot be tampered with. While there are exceptions to every rule, I don't think an Imperial Spell alone is one of them. (Perhaps in an elevated state such as Transcendence.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:20:05-07:00","id":1196015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1196012#post1196012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having both Ruling Arcana at 5 is enough. Prime 8 is hugely dominant in Supernal superiority, and so having equal or greater knowledge to the Mage in his own Ruling Path + Prime 8 can believably sever the connection.<br /> <br /> Requiring that three Arcana be 8 is such an insane requirement for a spell that effectively works on Mages only. Remember, Archmage's souls cannot be tampered with. While there are exceptions to every rule, I don't think an Imperial Spell alone is one of them. (Perhaps in an elevated state such as Transcendence.)</div> </div> </div> </div>These arguments make sense, yes. I will alter the spell slightly. Perhaps the archmage must be of the same Path, or have both ruling Arcana at 5 dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:30:38-07:00","id":1196019,"title":"","content":"This is just my 2 cents, but I'd make the requirements like this: Prime 8, and equal to / greater than dots in the Path arcanum of the target. <br /> <br /> If you want to Sever a Moros Master, that's Prime 8, Death 5, Matter 5<br /> <br /> Moros with Death 4, Matter 3? That's Prime 8, Death 4, Matter 3 minimum. In other words, you can't sever someone unless you have Prime 8 *and* know at least as much as they do about their own Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T04:20:36-07:00","id":1197935,"title":"","content":"I have updated the Annihilate Supernality spell as suggested. In the meantime, here are two more Prime spells. This also brings into question exactly how an Excision spell should affect targets. I've been designing the spells with the idea that Excision just straight up removes the relation of a target to the Arcanum, where as Entities can alter it (including reducing it), but never completely removing it. As an example, consider the difference between this spell and the Enlightenment spell I posted earlier.<br /> <br /> <b>Sever Arcanum</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Excision</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Subject\u2019s dots in Arcanum</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 4 Mana, 2 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> ???</li> </ul><br /> This spell removes the ability of a target to use an Arcanum. The archmaster must possess both Prime and the desired Arcanum at 7 dots. The subject loses all dots and Attainments in the Arcanum, and may never learn or utilize the Arcanum again. The subject cannot make use of imbued items or artifacts incorporating the Arcanum, and if a Prime spell grants them Mage Sight in the Arcanum, they cannot perceive the Supernal through that Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>Awaken</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Entities</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Resolve</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 4 Mana, 2 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A piece of a Watchtower, the soul of the subject from an alternate timeline where they Awakened</li> </ul><br /> The spell that all lesser mages wish they could have, but many archmasters resent having access to. By means of this spell, the archmaster Awakens a Sleeper to the full truth and power of magic. This subject of this spell immediately undergoes an Awakening. Once the Awakening begins, the ultimate fate of the subject is out of the archmaster\u2019s control. The subject\u2019s Path, what they do in the Supernal, and whether or not they actually manage to successfully Awaken or merely become a Sleepwalker are all beyond the reach of this spell. Use of this spell is one of the most dangerous and blatant violations of the Pax Arcanum: it almost always produces a Banisher, and attracts the attention of the Exarchs. With extensive preparation, it might be possible to reduce these dangers.<br /> <br /> <b>Add An Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022:</b> The archmaster may add up to three Arcana to the spell, granting these as the Ruling and Inferior Arcana for the new mage. These must be valid combinations of Arcana according to Path. For one Reach, the combination may be anything. If the archmaster does not add three Arcana, the Supernal chooses the rest.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster can at least guarantee that the subject will Awaken and become a mage.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster may target Sleepwalkers with this spell, giving them a second chance at Awakening.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T04:30:22-07:00","id":1197938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1197935#post1197935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> The archmaster may target Sleepwalkers with this spell, giving them a second chance at Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>A <i>second</i> chance at Awakening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T04:52:50-07:00","id":1197941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1197938#post1197938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A <i>second</i> chance at Awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepwalkers can be created when someone attempts to Awaken, and then fails. I suppose they can also be created without undergoing an Awakening at all, though. I think a lot of supernatural merits automatically also make the character a Sleepwalker too, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T05:28:28-07:00","id":1197946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1197941#post1197941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of supernatural merits automatically also make the character a Sleepwalker too, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any merit or lesser template, or other method which grants an inherent Supernatural power does.<br /> <br /> Owning a magic rod that can command animals? Not a Sleepwalker.<br /> Mystic ability to talk to Goldfish? Sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T08:57:42-07:00","id":1197991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1177212-creative-imperial-thaumaturgy?p=1197941#post1197941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepwalkers can be created when someone attempts to Awaken, and then fails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Sleepwalkers don't have that origin, and while the Supporting Cast appendix does mention that some Awakened thinks it's more difficult for people regularly exposed to the supernatural (such as Sleepwalkers with powers or non-powered Sleepwalkers who are introduced to Awakened society) to Awaken, it's actually not confirmed that is the case, and either way the given explanation wouldn't apply to this spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T01:11:59-07:00","id":1200732,"title":"","content":"<b>Shifting Flesh (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Entities</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 4 Mana, 2 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> The ephemeral remains of a slain Idigam, a species that has speciated within the last generation, the heart of a human with the Biokinesis and Biomimicry supernatural Merits.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> By embedding the chaos at the heart of the world\u2019s most adaptable lifeforms into another, the Archmaster grants a measure of that power to the target.<br /> <br /> The target effectively gains the Shifting Dread Power <b>(Werewolf: the Forsaken Second Edition, </b><i>p. 222)</i>, with the following modifications:<ul><li>The beneficiary\u2019s effective Rank is equal to the spell\u2019s Potency.</li> <li>Other than shifting dots (see below) the beneficiary can only benefit from one shift at a time.</li> <li>The beneficiary may only shift dots in physical attributes, physical skills, and merits that relate to a physical trait or skill (such as physical merits, most fighting styles, and some others such as Striking Looks). These shifts, once complete, are permanent. This does not allow the target to raise any attribute above their normal maximum.</li> <li>The target may not change Numen or other supernatural abilities.</li> <li>The target may additionally choose to heal damage equal to the spell's potency.</li> <li>When the beneficiary shifts to a particular form to help at a certain task, this always grants the +5 bonus as though they possessed the limited shifting ability.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Skills and attributes may be raised above the ordinary maximum, though any change above the maximum is never permanent and disappears - with the resulting dots being reassigned to a valid trait by the player - when the Shifting power is used again.<br /> <br /> A similar Entities spell exists for the Mind Arcanum, which is Withstood by Resolve and grants only the dot shifting ability, but allows this for any mental or social attribute, all skills, and any merit not reliant on either raw physical traits (such as Giant) or relations with others (such as Status, Allies or True Friend).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","user":"Mirthless","date":". 03-29-2018, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T01:28:52-07:00","id":1201186,"title":"","content":"This one is partly based on <b>Ascension</b>'s Augustine Aleph. <br /> <br /> <b>Universal Superior (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Resolve</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A proclamation granting wide powers to a certain individual, the soul of an absolute ruler.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> The Archmaster grasps the Supernal symbol of authority and shapes it to their own desire, granting its subject the same sovereign power over the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> This spell makes it so that the subject becomes the hierarchical superior to anyone they encounter. This grants effective Status dots in any organization whose member they interact with, at a level at least one higher than anyone in their immediate presence. Memories and possibility are no object: Any recollection is rewritten to suit, unless the victim\u2019s Resolve is high enough to Withstand the spell, and any impossibility is outright ignored: A mortal could easily be placed within the local vampiric hierarchy without so much as a passing comment. However, when the beneficiary of this spell interacts in ways that would ordinarily be impossible - such as trying to give orders to someone who truly has no superiors, or a female-presenting person giving orders within an all-male religious organization - this will make the effects fade quickly when outside of immediate range and likely trigger Quiescence.<br /> <br /> By default, this spell affects every organization the beneficiary interacts with. However, it is possible for an Archmaster to limit this spell\u2019s scope and immunize particular organizations or types thereof. This is often done to exempt supernatural organizations and prevent the inevitable backlash that would occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T03:16:02-07:00","id":1201196,"title":"","content":"Wait, how does Withstand work in these rules for Dynamics spells? Normally, it\u2019s the direct subject who Withstands. Can the secondary subjects of Dynamics (ie. subjects of the subject of a Dymamics spell) Withstand too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T04:12:56-07:00","id":1201202,"title":"","content":"I, uh...hadn't really considered it. With Withstand being a 2e mechanic absent in Imperial Mysteries, I guess there's really no canon answer (other than 'just like non-Imperial Practices', which would point to 'no'.)<br /> <br /> I instinctively went with yes, and I can think of two reasons, one based on the supposed way Dynamics works and another based on the every-tricky concept of 'balance':<br /> <br /> The first is that Dynamics spells are supposed to be magic that changes, grows and evolves to match changing circumstances. A fully working 'program' compared to the simple one-off 'functions' of spellcasting. This means that their powers can, in some circumstances, spread in nonstandard ways and indeed, this is how Universal Superior works: It uses the subject as a vector for a magic that temporarily overrules everyone's ordinary understanding of hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The second idea is that people <i>should</i> have the opportunity to resist their mental understanding of what is true being overridden and, since that cannot be at the moment of casting, this seemed the only other alternative.<br /> <br /> That said, these are not reasons I thought up when designing the spell, but post-hoc rationalizations to defend what I already did and as such the reasoning behind them is suspect and possibly faulty. As a counterpoint, the Mind spell 'Social Networking' doesn't seem to require any such Withstand, and in a lot of ways, it's a less-adaptable version of Universal Superior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T01:35:27-07:00","id":1201566,"title":"","content":"The following two are not so much spells as enhancements to existing spells, based on Hung Spell in the core but adapted to the scale on which Archmasters work. The Fate spell is actually an Attainment in my own half-finished Imperial Mysteries patch (which draws heavily on Falco\u2019s work).<br /> <br /> <b>Imperial Trigger (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> None (though the component spells do; see below)</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> The disruption of an otherwise balanced system, a response system to an action that would otherwise be cataclysmic.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> The Archmaster crafts a spell container of sorts, which regulates the status of other spells contained within it.<br /> <br /> Once this spell is cast it may embed one or more spells (as per its Scale) which must all have the same target or targets, giving them a number of trigger conditions equal to its Potency. These trigger conditions may freely interact with any of the spells (giving them separate or identical triggers) and with each other (thus creating conditions which are dependent on other conditions). The triggers are dynamic, capable of operating on any trigger that the Mage could detect with any sense or through Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> If Imperial Trigger ends before its component spells do, the components are left in the condition they are in at the duration (effectively ending the spell if it is left \u2018off\u2019). If the component spells end before the Imperial Trigger does, the spells simply end.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Any Arcanum 2: </b>The triggers may also operate on any information the Mage could get through any Knowing or Unveiling spell of that Arcanum.<br /> <b>Add Time 4: </b>The time spent inactive by component spells does not count towards their duration.<br /> <br /> <i>Example: An Imperial Trigger is cast with Potency 5 and the embedded spells Body Control, Heightened Senses, Mend, and Life Force Assault. Its triggers are:</i><ul><li><i>Body Control and Mend are active whenever the target actively works towards the Mage\u2019s goals.</i></li> <li><i>Heightened Senses functions when the target desires it to.</i></li> <li><i>Mend has an additional trigger that it only functions when not in view of Sleepers.</i></li> <li><i>Body Control, Heightened Senses and Mend all stop working whenever the target stops considering themselves a loyal servant to the Archmaster and will not reactivate until they do.</i></li> <li><i>Finally, if the target takes violent action against the Mage, Life Force Assault activates and all benefits permanently stop, unable to be reactivated.</i></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Adaptive Scaling (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Dynamics</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 2 Mana</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> None (though the component spells do; see below)</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A complete organizational chart of a multinational corporation, a genealogy going back at least ten generations</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> The Archmaster has developed the ability to cast spells which dynamically affect a certain group defined by their Sympathetic links. The Archmaster may include spells with a total number of dots equal to the spell\u2019s Potency. These spells must all initially affect the same targets as the spell\u2019s Scale.<br /> <br /> When adaptive scaling is cast, define a group of people encompassed by the spell, such as the members of an organization or the descendants of a particular person. Once the spell is cast, the component spells\u2019 scaling dynamically adjusts to encompass any changes in the defined target: People who are no longer members of an organization are no longer affected while new people joining gain the effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T00:35:19-07:00","id":1202479,"title":"","content":"<b>Annihilate Banes (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022)</b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Excision</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 4 Mana, 2 Arcane Beats</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Rank</li> <li><b>Example Quintessences:</b> A fatal flaw that causes a building or organization to collapse</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> The Mage scours the target\u2019s pattern, ripping out the Spirit\u2019s Ban or Bane and removing it entirely. This affects the Spirit so blessed in all expected ways: a bane no longer does damage to the creature, while an action taken can no longer be against its ban. Removing either the Ban or Bane also makes it impossible to ward against the spirit.<br /> <br /> If any action is taken that would impose a new or different ban or bane, the spell goes into a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell applies to both the ban and the bane instead of one or the other.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell also works against any ban or bane imposed due to superior Rank.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Instead of removing the ban or bane entirely, the Archmaster creates a new, hidden one. This ban or bane cannot be researched, and the spell Clashes with any supernatural ability to discern it. By default, only the caster is aware of the new weakness. Used in this way, the spell is an Entities spell.<br /> <br /> Death and Mind variants of this spell exist, removing the bans or banes of Ghosts and Goetia respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T05:30:41-07:00","id":1202529,"title":"","content":"These are some great spells.<br /> <br /> Entities and Excision spells are said to be Lasting duration in Imperial Mysteries, so I'm not sure Clash of Wills is appropriate for them, unless the Clash is built directly into the effect of the Entities/Excision spell itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}